= High Human Culture

[? if hhc_kind = "core" : On Corulag and Coruscant, the "High Human Culture" societies fill their halls. Their speakers tell well-dressed crowds that humans built the Republic and that the "anti-humans" in the Rim threaten the Republic itself. Their pamphlets praise [+ pal_title +] as a man willing to stand up to the alien. ?][? if hhc_kind = "senate" : A human-first club has formed among the Core's delegations. Its members vote together, dine together, and toast "the founding peoples". Several non-human senators find their committee seats quietly reassigned. ?][? if hhc_kind = "military" : In the Navy's officer messes, the toast is to "High Human Culture". Non-human officers find their promotions delayed and their postings remote, and the admirals who arrange it are spoken of as the Republic's future. ?]

On the Rim, the speeches are replayed with a different commentary: this is what the Core thinks of you.
